spec: S30-01, S30-03

`password` on a stopped data dir: `--clear` removes every Member's local password, so a browser
on the machine is trusted as the owner again; TTY and non-TTY; `--json ?`; a store held by a
running server is refused (here: the harness's own store in `~/.annotary`).

```console
$ ANNOTARY_HOME=pwhome ANNOTARY_SETUP_HANDLE=rowan ANNOTARY_SETUP_NAME=Rowan ANNOTARY_SETUP_PASSWORD=hunter2 annotary -q serve --setup-only
? success
...

$ ANNOTARY_HOME=pwhome ANNOTARY_TTY=1 annotary --no-color password --clear
MEMBER  PASSWORD
@rowan  removed
password: no local password is set — a browser on this machine is trusted as the owner

$ ANNOTARY_HOME=pwhome annotary password --clear
password: no local password to remove

$ ANNOTARY_HOME=pwhome ANNOTARY_PASSWORD=hunter2 annotary password --set
new local password for @rowan: ********
@rowan	set

$ ANNOTARY_HOME=pwhome annotary password --clear --json ?
member password id store

$ annotary password --clear
? 5
error: store [..] is locked by another annotary serve (pid [..]) — stop it first, or use --data-dir / ANNOTARY_HOME for a separate store

```
